Cloud environments should evolve continuously to meet changing business requirements. Service improvement planning identifies opportunities to enhance reliability, security, performance, and operational efficiency.

Improvement initiatives may include:

* Infrastructure optimization
* Security enhancements
* Cost reduction
* Automation
* Documentation updates
* Staff training
* Process refinement

For example, repeated operational incidents may indicate that additional automation or updated monitoring rules are required.

A real-life use case is organizations conducting quarterly service improvement workshops based on operational metrics and customer feedback.

Structured improvement planning supports long-term cloud maturity.
